  <body>
    <div class="cover">
      <div class="company">SALE FISH MARKETING AND CONSULTING</div>
      <div class="tagline">OT Cybersecurity Practice</div>
      <div class="title">OT Cybersecurity<br/>Assessment Report</div>
      <p style="margin-top:30pt; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold;">Lake Charles Pipeline Station</p>
      <p style="font-size:11pt;">Meridian Midstream LLC</p>
      <p style="margin-top:20pt; font-size:12pt;">Oil &amp; Gas &nbsp;|&nbsp; TSA Pipeline Security Directives</p>
      <p style="font-size:11pt; color:#595959;">November 21, 2026</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-break"></div>
    <h1>Executive Summary</h1>
    <table class="meta-table">
      <tr><td class="meta-label">Site:</td><td>Lake Charles Pipeline Station</td><td class="meta-label">Organization:</td><td>Meridian Midstream LLC</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="meta-label">Industry:</td><td>Oil &amp; Gas</td><td class="meta-label">Standard:</td><td>TSA Pipeline Security Directives</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="meta-label">Assessment Mode:</td><td>Detailed</td><td class="meta-label">Date:</td><td>November 21, 2026</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="meta-label">Assessor:</td><td>T. Jackson, Sale Fish Marketing and Consulting</td><td class="meta-label">Question Bank:</td><td>v2.1.0</td></tr>
    </table>

    <div style="margin-top:14pt;">
      <div class="kpi-box"><div class="val">2.9</div><div class="lbl">Overall Maturity (CMM 1-5)</div></div>
      <div class="kpi-box"><div class="val">3.0</div><div class="lbl">Risk-Weighted Maturity</div></div>
      <div class="kpi-box"><div class="val">3.3</div><div class="lbl">Industry Baseline (Illustrative)</div></div>
      <div class="kpi-box"><div class="val">11</div><div class="lbl">Risk Items Identified</div></div>
    </div>

    
    <p><strong>Lake Charles Pipeline Station</strong> (Meridian Midstream LLC) — This assessment evaluated <strong>Oil &amp; Gas</strong> OT cybersecurity maturity against <strong>TSA Pipeline Security Directives</strong>, cross-referenced to NIST CSF 2.0, using the detailed question set.</p>
    <p>Overall maturity scored <strong>2.9 out of 5.0 (Managed)</strong>, below the illustrative Oil &amp; Gas sector baseline of 3.3. The risk-weighted maturity score is <strong>3.0</strong>.</p>
    <p>The weakest NIST CSF 2.0 function is <strong>Identify</strong> (2.3/5), warranting priority attention. A total of <strong>11 risk item(s)</strong> scored at or below 3.0 and are prioritized in the Top 10 Risks section below.</p>
    <p style="color:var(--text-muted); font-size:13px;">Assessed by: T. Jackson, Sale Fish Marketing and Consulting</p>
  
    <p class="note">N/A responses were excluded from scoring averages for this report. Industry baseline is an illustrative planning estimate, not empirical survey data.</p>

    <div class="page-break"></div>
    <h1>Detailed Summary</h1>
    <h2>Control Family Maturity</h2>
    <img class="chart-img" src="data:image/png;base64," width="600" style="width:600px;" />
    <table class="report-table"><tr><th>ID</th><th>Control Family</th><th>NIST CSF 2.0 Cross-Reference</th><th>CTRL Ref</th><th>Score</th><th>CMM Level</th></tr>
    <tr>
      <td>SEG</td><td>IT/OT Network Segmentation</td><td>PR.IR — Technology Infrastructure Resilience</td>
      <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace; font-size:8.5pt;">CTRL-3.2.1, CTRL-3.3.1</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">3.5</td>
      <td>Defined</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>ACC</td><td>Access Control &amp; MFA</td><td>PR.AA — Identity Management, Authentication and Access Control</td>
      <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace; font-size:8.5pt;">CTRL-3.3.2, CTRL-3.3.3</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">3.5</td>
      <td>Defined</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>PATCH</td><td>Patch &amp; Vulnerability Management</td><td>ID.RA — Risk Assessment</td>
      <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace; font-size:8.5pt;">CTRL-4.3.1, CTRL-4.3.2, CTRL-8.2.1</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">2.5</td>
      <td>Managed</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>MON</td><td>Continuous Monitoring</td><td>DE.CM — Continuous Monitoring</td>
      <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace; font-size:8.5pt;">CTRL-6.1.1, CTRL-6.1.2, CTRL-6.4.1</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">3.0</td>
      <td>Defined</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>IRPT</td><td>Incident Reporting &amp; Response</td><td>RS.MA — Incident Management</td>
      <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace; font-size:8.5pt;">CTRL-7.1.2</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">2.5</td>
      <td>Managed</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>CIP</td><td>Cybersecurity Implementation Plan / Governance</td><td>GV.RR — Roles, Responsibilities, and Authorities</td>
      <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace; font-size:8.5pt;">—</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">3.5</td>
      <td>Defined</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>TPA</td><td>Cybersecurity Assessment Program</td><td>ID.IM — Improvement</td>
      <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace; font-size:8.5pt;">—</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">2.0</td>
      <td>Managed</td>
    </tr></table>

    <h2>NIST CSF 2.0 Function Rollup</h2>
    <img class="chart-img" src="data:image/png;base64," width="380" style="width:380px;" />
    <table class="report-table"><tr><th>CSF 2.0 Function</th><th>Average Score</th></tr><tr><td>Govern (GV)</td><td style="text-align:center;">3.5</td></tr><tr><td>Identify (ID)</td><td style="text-align:center;">2.3</td></tr><tr><td>Protect (PR)</td><td style="text-align:center;">3.5</td></tr><tr><td>Detect (DE)</td><td style="text-align:center;">3.0</td></tr><tr><td>Respond (RS)</td><td style="text-align:center;">2.5</td></tr><tr><td>Recover (RC)</td><td style="text-align:center;">—</td></tr></table>

    <h2>Maturity vs. Industry Baseline</h2>
    <img class="chart-img" src="data:image/png;base64," width="600" style="width:600px;" />

    <div class="page-break"></div>
    <h1>Top 10 Risks (Prioritized)</h1>
    <p class="note">Priority score = (5 − control score) × control-family criticality weight.</p>
    <table class="report-table"><tr><th>#</th><th>Control Family</th><th>Item</th><th>Score</th><th>Recommended Action</th></tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">1</td><td>Incident Reporting &amp; Response</td><td>Incident response roles and escalation paths are defined and rehearsed, not only documented on paper.</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">2/5</td><td>Document and rehearse a process ensuring qualifying incidents are reported to CISA within the required timeframe. Define and rehearse incident response roles and escalation paths.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">2</td><td>Patch &amp; Vulnerability Management</td><td>Compensating controls are documented and applied for vulnerabilities that cannot be immediately patched.</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">2/5</td><td>Document a risk-based patch management process (deliberate, tracked, not necessarily immediate). Maintain documented compensating controls for vulnerabilities that cannot be immediately patched.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">3</td><td>Cybersecurity Assessment Program</td><td>The effectiveness of the measures in the Cybersecurity Implementation Plan is assessed on the required cadence, including an architectural design review, by assessors independent of the team implementing them.</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">2/5</td><td>Run the TSA-required Cybersecurity Assessment Program on its required cadence, including the architectural design review, with assessors independent of the team implementing the controls and findings tracked to closure with assigned ownership and timelines.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">4</td><td>Cybersecurity Assessment Program</td><td>Assessment findings are tracked to closure with assigned ownership and timelines.</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">2/5</td><td>Run the TSA-required Cybersecurity Assessment Program on its required cadence, including the architectural design review, with assessors independent of the team implementing the controls and findings tracked to closure with assigned ownership and timelines.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">5</td><td>IT/OT Network Segmentation</td><td>Segmentation architecture is documented and available for TSA/CISA review upon request.</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">3/5</td><td>Document a formal industrial DMZ / segmentation architecture separating IT and OT, and keep the documentation current for TSA/CISA review.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">6</td><td>Incident Reporting &amp; Response</td><td>A documented process ensures qualifying incidents are reported to CISA within the required timeframe.</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">3/5</td><td>Document and rehearse a process ensuring qualifying incidents are reported to CISA within the required timeframe. Define and rehearse incident response roles and escalation paths.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">7</td><td>Access Control &amp; MFA</td><td>Remote access sessions are logged, time-boxed, and reviewed.</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">3/5</td><td>Enforce MFA for all remote access, including vendor/OEM support sessions. Log, time-box, and review all remote access sessions.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">8</td><td>Continuous Monitoring</td><td>Continuous monitoring capability is deployed across OT network segments, not only at the IT/OT boundary.</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">3/5</td><td>Deploy continuous monitoring capability broadly across OT network segments, not just at the IT/OT boundary. Establish a defined review cadence and escalation path for monitoring findings.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">9</td><td>Continuous Monitoring</td><td>Monitoring findings are reviewed on a defined cadence with a documented escalation path.</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">3/5</td><td>Deploy continuous monitoring capability broadly across OT network segments, not just at the IT/OT boundary. Establish a defined review cadence and escalation path for monitoring findings.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">10</td><td>Patch &amp; Vulnerability Management</td><td>A documented, risk-based patch management process is in place and followed (not necessarily immediate, but deliberate and tracked).</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">3/5</td><td>Document a risk-based patch management process (deliberate, tracked, not necessarily immediate). Maintain documented compensating controls for vulnerabilities that cannot be immediately patched.</td>
    </tr></table>

