    <h1>Full Assessment Detail (Appendix)</h1>
    <p class="note">Every question and response, including items that scored above the risk threshold.</p>
    <table class="report-table"><tr><th>Family</th><th>Question</th><th>Score</th><th>Notes</th></tr><tr><td>SEG</td><td>OT is segmented from IT via a documented architecture (industrial DMZ or equivalent), not a flat or loosely-firewalled network.</td><td style="text-align:center;">4</td><td>Segmentation architecture documented in the TSA-approved CIP; one undocumented cellular modem found on the metering skid.</td></tr><tr><td>SEG</td><td>Segmentation architecture is documented and available for TSA/CISA review upon request.</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td>Segmentation architecture documented in the TSA-approved CIP; one undocumented cellular modem found on the metering skid.</td></tr><tr><td>ACC</td><td>MFA is enforced for all remote access into the OT environment, including vendor/OEM support sessions.</td><td style="text-align:center;">4</td><td>MFA enforced on VPN and PAM. Session recording on, but recordings aren't reviewed.</td></tr><tr><td>ACC</td><td>Remote access sessions are logged, time-boxed, and reviewed.</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td>MFA enforced on VPN and PAM. Session recording on, but recordings aren't reviewed.</td></tr><tr><td>PATCH</td><td>A documented, risk-based patch management process is in place and followed (not necessarily immediate, but deliberate and tracked).</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td>Risk-based patching documented; compensating controls not recorded for the 14 deferred items.</td></tr><tr><td>PATCH</td><td>Compensating controls are documented and applied for vulnerabilities that cannot be immediately patched.</td><td style="text-align:center;">2</td><td>Risk-based patching documented; compensating controls not recorded for the 14 deferred items.</td></tr><tr><td>MON</td><td>Continuous monitoring capability is deployed across OT network segments, not only at the IT/OT boundary.</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>MON</td><td>Monitoring findings are reviewed on a defined cadence with a documented escalation path.</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>IRPT</td><td>A documented process ensures qualifying incidents are reported to CISA within the required timeframe.</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td>CIRP still references the 24-hour window; needs updating for SD Pipeline-2021-01G (72 hours).</td></tr><tr><td>IRPT</td><td>Incident response roles and escalation paths are defined and rehearsed, not only documented on paper.</td><td style="text-align:center;">2</td><td>CIRP still references the 24-hour window; needs updating for SD Pipeline-2021-01G (72 hours).</td></tr><tr><td>CIP</td><td>A current, TSA-approved Cybersecurity Implementation Plan exists describing how each directive requirement is met.</td><td style="text-align:center;">4</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>CIP</td><td>Senior management accountability for cybersecurity is documented and exercised, not nominal, including a designated Cybersecurity Coordinator.</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>TPA</td><td>The effectiveness of the measures in the Cybersecurity Implementation Plan is assessed on the required cadence, including an architectural design review, by assessors independent of the team implementing them.</td><td style="text-align:center;">2</td><td>Architectural design review overdue (last performed 2024). Assessment findings tracked in a spreadsheet with no owners.</td></tr><tr><td>TPA</td><td>Assessment findings are tracked to closure with assigned ownership and timelines.</td><td style="text-align:center;">2</td><td>Architectural design review overdue (last performed 2024). Assessment findings tracked in a spreadsheet with no owners.</td></tr></table>

    
